Test the echo taken to be no louder than the microphone heard after aligning anew

WebRTC patch 0018 caps the echo path gain of AEC3's non-linear echo model after the
echo controller is aligned anew, at what the microphone heard against the render, until
the linear filter takes over. In test/echo_aligned_anew.test.cc AEC3 hears a room's echo
of the other side's voice, 20 dB under it, and the output changes four times
(RestartForOtherDevices), to an echo 120 ms later and back or to the same delay; a word
of the person's own, 0.5 to 1.1 s after each change, comes out at least 0.3 dB less held
down than with the cap left out (Fogata-Aec3EchoPathGainCapAfterAligningAnew/0/, stock
AEC3), and the echo without the word no louder than 1 dB over stock's at its loudest 100
ms in the 3.3 s after each change. With an echo 6 dB under the other side's voice, the
echo is no louder than stock's and the word no more than 0.5 dB more held down. Built in
again: the library shows only its own API.

